cuems-videocomposer (0.1.2-10) unstable; urgency=high

  * Frame pacing: coupled pacing (every output presents on the slowest
    CRTC's vblank, one atomic commit for all) is the default again.
    Per-surface pacing (PR #8, 869emcrwa) shipped as default in 0.1.2-9 and
    regressed multi-output playback: the loop woke once per CRTC flip, the
    MTC rate estimator sampled 10 ms head steps across 1-5 ms sibling wakes
    and the smooth clock was hard-snapped back 11 ms several times a second
    (`MIDISync: anti-drift SNAP errorMs=-11`), and the cadence smoother
    counted those wakes as vsyncs and lost its minimum hold. Per-surface
    pacing stays opt-in: VIDEOCOMPOSER_PER_SURFACE_PACING=1 (mixed-refresh
    canvases only, not yet validated for stutter-free playback).
    VIDEOCOMPOSER_COUPLED_PACING=1 still forces coupled.
  * MIDISyncSource: the MTC rate is sampled over >= 500 ms windows and
    clamped to +-5 % (independent of the poll cadence); also removes the rare
    +11..+19 ms snaps 0.1.2-6 logged at 2x4K30.
  * Regression test Integration_MIDISyncSource_RateWindowImmuneToPollCadence
    (fails on the 0.1.2-9 estimator, passes here; suite 100/100 on an N97).
  * Verified by eye on .111 (2026-10-20): stock 0.1.2-9 with two outputs
    shows the jumps; this build plays a 60 fps clip over three decoding
    layers on a single matched output without a hitch.
  * Analysis: cuems-RELATIONS Plans/2026-10-20-vc-per-surface-pacing-
    stutter-review.md. FP530 operators: a mixed-refresh canvas is back on
    the pre-PR #8 behaviour (paced by the slowest CRTC) unless opted in.

 -- Ion Reguera <ion@stagelab.coop>  Mon, 20 Oct 2026 20:30:00 +0200

cuems-videocomposer (0.1.2-9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * FP530 campaign (ClickUp 869en65tm; PR #8, supersedes #2):
    - Per-CRTC frame pacing: each refresh-rate class flips on its own vblank,
      so mixed refresh rates no longer break the canvas (869emcrwa).
    - Decode path: the synchronous decoder is gone (probe context only,
      freed at once) - one hardware decode context per layer instead of two.
      An 8 GB FP530 now survives a 4-layer fade show for 5 h; 0.1.2-7
      starved it in 14 min.
    - G12 hang guard, saturation monitor and machine profiles (keyed on the
      GPU). The cue refusal is OFF by default: --hang-guard=on enforces the
      measured cap, --hang-guard=off disarms everything; counts, advisories
      and saturation warnings always run.
    - The compositor's death is reported (exit reporter); recovery-policy
      tests.

