cuems-videocomposer (0.1.2-5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Build-Depends declared three packages that do not exist in Debian
    (libopenmp-dev, libva-drm2-dev, libva-x11-2-dev), so dpkg-checkbuilddeps
    refused every build unless -d was passed. The libva pair was redundant
    too — libva-dev, already listed, ships all three VA headers — and OpenMP
    is an optional find_package() satisfied by g++'s own libgomp. Removed;
    dpkg-checkbuilddeps now passes.
  * test_VideoLayer_SyncUpdate had failed since layers stopped following MTC
    by default, forcing 0.1.2-4 to be built with DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS=nocheck.
    The default is correct (the engine sends /mtcfollow at the cue start), so
    the test was stale; it now enables MTC following before asserting.
    Suite: 32 passed, 0 failed. This release builds with tests enabled.

 -- Ion Reguera <ion@stagelab.coop>  Fri, 14 Aug 2026 20:22:10 +0200

cuems-videocomposer (0.1.2-4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * display.conf per-output keys are applied instead of merely parsed.
    enabled=, refresh= and resolution= were read into OutputConfiguration
    and never consulted by anything that sets a mode, so a connected but
    unwanted output could not be left dark and a refresh rate could not be
    requested. A disabled output now gets no surface at all (no GBM/EGL, no
    CRTC, no modeset) and no canvas region; an explicit refresh= is honoured
    and pins that output out of refresh-rate harmonization, which otherwise
    raised it straight back to the highest common rate. A requested mode
    that does not exist now fails loudly instead of dropping silently to the
    EDID preferred one. Verified on FP530: 30Hz requested and achieved on a
    pinned output while an unpinned one stayed at 60Hz.
    (ClickUp 869efh2hr, 869efhv04)
  * A video file that fails to open now says why: av_strerror text, which
    FFmpeg call refused, and the on-disk size, instead of one identical
    "Failed to open" line for six unrelated causes. (ClickUp 869efh2ma)

  * NOTE for upgrades: resolution= and refresh= were inert until now, so an
    existing display.conf may carry stale values that become live with this
    package. Audit per-output sections before upgrading a host.

